<title>NETHERLANDS: VENTURE CAPITAL ROLE FOR EIB IN EU ACCORD -OFFICIAL.</title>
<headline>VENTURE CAPITAL ROLE FOR EIB IN EU ACCORD -OFFICIAL.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union finance ministers agreed on Monday to involve the European Investment Bank in venture capital for the first time, Catherine Colonna, spokeswoman for French President Jacques Chirac, said.</p>
<p>&quot;The ministers agreed that the EIB should study creating a facility to help small businesses innovate in high technology,&quot; she told a news conference after the ministers met during a summit of EU leaders in Amsterdam.</p>
<p>&quot;This could involve for the first time the EIB taking stakes in the form of risk capital in targeted projects,&quot; she added.</p>
</text>
